From: haiku-rpi
Subject: [PATCH] video: bcm2835: request the BGR pixel order that U-Boot and its EFI GOP assume

U-Boot draws 32-bit pixels as 0x00RRGGBB (blue in the low byte) and its EFI GOP
reports EFI_GOT_BGRA8, but the framebuffer was requested in RGB order (red in the
low byte), so EFI applications (Haiku) showed red and blue swapped.
---
diff --git a/drivers/video/bcm2835.c b/drivers/video/bcm2835.c
index 0e0cc197..e174232b 100644
--- a/drivers/video/bcm2835.c
+++ b/drivers/video/bcm2835.c
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ static int bcm2835_video_probe(struct udevice *dev)
 		return -EIO;
 
 	debug("bcm2835: Setting up display for %d x %d\n", w, h);
-	ret = bcm2835_set_video_params(&w, &h, 32, BCM2835_MBOX_PIXEL_ORDER_RGB,
+	ret = bcm2835_set_video_params(&w, &h, 32, BCM2835_MBOX_PIXEL_ORDER_BGR,
 				       BCM2835_MBOX_ALPHA_MODE_IGNORED,
 				       &fb_base, &fb_size, &pitch);
 	if (ret)
